@appendixsubsec User options

@defopt vm-assimilate-html-command
@vindex vm-assimilate-html-command
Command/function which should be called for stripping tags.

When this is a string, then it is a command which is fed with the
html and which should return the text.
Otherwise it should be a Lisp function which performs the stripping of
the tags.

I prefer to use lynx for this job:

#!/bin/tcsh

tmpfile=/tmp/$USER-striptags.html
cat > $tmpfile
lynx -force_html -dump $tmpfile
rm $tmpfile

Default value: @code{"striptags"}
@end defopt

@defopt vm-assimilate-html-mixed
@vindex vm-assimilate-html-mixed
Non-nil values cause messages to be assimilated as text/mixed.
Otherwise they will be assimilated into a text/alternative message.

Default value: @code{t}
@end defopt

@defopt vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-charset
@vindex vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-charset
The default charset used for attached files of type @code{text}.
If set to nil you will be asked for the charset.
If set to @code{guess} it will be determined by @code{vm-determine-proper-charset}, but
this may take some time, since the file needs to be visited.

Default value: @code{guess}
@end defopt

@defopt vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-type
@vindex vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-type
The default MIME-type for attached files.
If set to nil you will be asked for the type if it cannot be guessed.
For guessing mime-types we use @code{vm-mime-attachment-auto-type-alist}.
@end defopt

@defopt vm-enable-addons
@vindex vm-enable-addons
A list of addons to enable, t for all and nil to disable all.
Most addons are from @code{vm-rfaddons-infect-vm}.

You must restart VM after a change to cause any effects.

Default value: @code{(check-for-empty-subject encode-headers)}
@end defopt

@defopt vm-handle-return-receipt-mode
@vindex vm-handle-return-receipt-mode
Tells @code{vm-handle-return-receipt} how to handle return receipts.
One can choose between @code{ask}, @code{auto}, @code{edit}, or an expression which should
return t if the return receipts should be sent.

Default value: @code{edit}
